notes.body:
Hi João, great new feature, it has been on my wishlist for a long time. A usecase for me would be something like:

  with http.cookie contains "XXX" as COOKIES then tcp.stream == @{COOKIES:tcp.stream}

I tried with a simple trace containing an HTTP POST with the following filter:

  with http.request.method==POST as POSTS then tcp.stream == @{POSTS:tcp.stream}

It did not show the full TCP stream, just the packets from the TCP stream from the packet having the POST onwards. I assume that this is 'works-as-designed' to prevent a 3rd filtering pass. However, I think a filter like mine should indeed show all packets of the tcp stream, including the ones before the packet(s) matching the first fitler.

What do you think?

@SYN-bit I updated the MR, can you check if it does what you want?

The implementation now does two passes over the capture file, to provide for back references.

I can imagine it being useful to extract streams from a single field.

